<Section id="circles" title="2. Plotting Points with Circles">

Now we draw inside the canvas. A point is a `<circle>`, which needs a centre (`cx`, `cy`) and a radius `r`:

```svelte
/// file: A circle
<svg class="chart" width="500" height="350">
	<circle cx="50" cy={350 - 70} r="8" fill="steelblue" />
</svg>
```

To draw the circle:
- We start with placing the circle at the correct position with `cx` and `cy` and then 
- `r` - gives it a radius.
- `fill` to make it visible. This can be any colour eg. "red", "#ff0000", hsl(0, 100%, 50%), etc.

<Exercise file="1-first-scatter-plot.svelte">
	<FirstScatterPlot />
	{#snippet result()}
		<ScatterDemo />
	{/snippet}
</Exercise>

{#snippet sidebar()}

> [!Note] Handy extras
> - **Complex math**: use curly brackets to compute a value inline — `cy={350 - 70}` is just 70 up from the bottom.
> - **Outlines**: add `stroke` (outline colour) and `stroke-width` (thickness) to give a circle a border.

```svelte
/// file: Circle
<circle cx="50" cy={350 - 70} r="8" fill="steelblue" stroke="white" stroke-width="2" />
```

**RESULT**:

